{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"actinium-civic-needletail","creation_channel":"cli","description":"The 'main Gerrit Verified Gate' workflow's macOS pytest job has a post-test step 'Report and release macOS default-suite pytest tree' that runs 'rm -rf' over the pytest RAM-disk basetemp. The snapshot tests (tests covering .rebar/run_snapshots, e.g. test_snapshot_is_read_only, test_snapshot_extracts_tracked) legitimately create read-only snapshot trees (0555 dirs / 0444 files). On macOS BSD 'rm', files inside a read-only directory cannot be unlinked ('Permission denied'), so the directory stays 'Directory not empty' and the step exits 1 EVEN THOUGH pytest itself passed (13393 passed, 65 skipped). This is intermittent (depends on which worker/snapshots land on the RAM disk) and blocks the Verified vote for otherwise-green changes. Fix: make the cleanup 'chmod -R u+w' the tree before 'rm -rf' (or use 'chflags -R nouchg' + 'rm -rf'), mirroring how the snapshot tests' own teardown restores perms. Observed on change 1808 patchsets 1 and 2 (3 consecutive macOS runs); recent unrelated changes pass the same job, confirming it is environmental, not change-specific.","id":"b5e6-a289-e51b-41b2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"macOS Verified-gate cleanup step fails on read-only run_snapshots dirs"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786782916770291001,"uuid":"ff0c4bd7-b91c-48a0-a336-4cd1c06136f7"}